  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F. Mix the chili powder, paprika, onion powder, garlic powder, cumin, cayenne, sugar, and salt in a small bowl.",
    "Cut the onions and bell peppers into 1/4-inch strips. Slice the chicken into thin strips. Put the chicken and vegetables on a large rimmed baking sheet.",
    "Drizzle with the oil, sprinkle the seasoning over, and toss with your hands until everything is coated. Spread into an even layer.",
    "Bake 35-40 min, stirring once halfway, until the vegetables are tender and browned at the edges and the thickest chicken strip reads 165°F.",
    "Squeeze the juice of half the lime over the pan as it comes out of the oven. Cut the other half into wedges.",
    "Warm the tortillas, fill each with some chicken and vegetables, and top with cilantro sprigs, a spoonful of sour cream, and an extra squeeze of lime."
  ],
